# The inbox state is read beside the catalog: a thread the web app already
# holds a snooze for (seeded an hour ahead of the pinned clock) shows
# "Snoozed until <due>" in its row menu without any local act; a thread
# whose snooze is already past due shows Snooze again (the model says it
# woke), and nothing in the list moved.
# The runner pins TZ=UTC and HANABI_MOCK_NOW=1781524800 (12:00Z); the labels
# below are those instants in that zone. t6 is due 13:00Z (pending); t7 was
# due 11:59Z (past: the menu says Snooze again, never the stale row). Rows
# are addressed by id, not by a coordinate: with both threads seeded the
# list order is not the other scripts'. Assertions do not block the next
# command (runner.h dispatches every tick) and retry for MAX_FRAMES=30
# (pending_command.h) before they fail, so the menu is held open for 32
# frames after each one before the Escape that would close what it reads.
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_MOCK_SNOOZES=t6:1781528400:1781524740,t7:1781524740:1781520000
wait_frames 20
expect_text "SKU backfill — my name for it"
expect_text "coordinating 3 shard workers"
right_click_ui chat_row_id_t6
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Snoozed until 1:00 PM"
wait_frames 32
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 4
right_click_ui chat_row_id_t7
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Snooze"
expect_no_text "Snoozed until"
expect_no_text "11:59 AM"
wait_frames 32
key ESCAPE
